query: >-
  Show the implemented Analyze MP3 request and response sequence through the browser, NGINX, native raw bridge, real
  Fastify root, scoped upload plugin and pure parser. Separate page components, the upload-state hook and raw service.
  The factory registers root schemas/canonical errors and Swagger before sibling upload/health plugins. Accepted
  uploads enter Fastify onRequest admission before allocation, then the scoped bounded content parser and MP3 route.
  The route analyzes once, projects only allowed fields and checks aggregate invariants before schema serialization.
  Raw refusals and incomplete-native-body draining use the same catalogue projection. Release buffers, deadlines and
  admission once through handler finally, rejection and terminal hooks; disconnected clients have no JSON guarantee.
  Include local file validation, pending controls, the actual-byte 20 MiB bound and typed parser failures.
  Limit the JSON ingress-error branch to configured 413, 502 and 504 mappings. Separate response JSON validation from
  other ingress responses without a JSON guarantee; unreadable JSON becomes a readable error. Separate this from
  rejected fetches handled by the hook's timeout/network catch. Render current outcomes, ignore stale completions and
  clear every admitted request's deadline in finally. Walk complete MPEG-1 Layer III frames; exclude only a recognized
  leading Xing/Info carrier from audio count, retaining physical/excluded diagnostics. Declared totals never determine
  the result. Shared schemas/code catalogue govern default/details and errors. Aborts never produce partial success.
  Use the referenced implementation at the current revision as runtime authority. Historical architecture snapshots
  remain historical evidence. This diagram describes the local application, not a cloud deployment.
  Group NGINX inside the frontend Docker container and API plus parser inside the API Docker container. The API and
  parser share one Node process; browser JavaScript runs outside Docker. Never draw the parser as a third container.
